  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Routing budget",
      "items": [
        "Default routing budget 10000 ms (routingTimeoutMs)",
        "Dual-backend: Laya gets floor(remaining × ¾) — 7500 ms at defaults, reserving a quarter for Jev",
        "Sole backend receives the full remaining budget",
        "Attempts are sequential; the first valid typed choice ends routing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust and isolation",
      "items": [
        "Hosted Jev requires all three gates: config enabled, TURNHELM_ALLOW_HOSTED_JEV=1, non-empty TYPESAFE_API_KEY",
        "Worker child env strips routing credentials; ZDOTDIR redirects to the managed .turnhelm root so zsh descendants skip host startup files",
        "Every run builds a fresh per-run CODEX_HOME (--ephemeral, --ignore-user-config, --ignore-rules); a run with no discoverable credential is refused before classification, and receipts attest codexHomeManaged",
        "TURNHELM_MANAGED_CHILD=1 blocks recursion; sandbox read-only unless --write, at most one worker per run"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Task entry and evidence",
      "items": [
        "Task limited to 8192 UTF-8 bytes via argv or stdin; continuation-only prompts rejected",
        "--output-schema validates the caller's file once at the boundary and stages the bytes inside the managed home — the caller's path is never forwarded",
        "Stdout carries at most one message — the final agent message of a completed run, classified at emission as strict, extracted, conflict, or unstructured; no write starts once failure or cancellation is observed (delivery is not transactional)",
        "Exactly one turnhelm.receipt on stderr once classification starts",
        "routes.jsonl journals the task SHA-256, decision, and classifier confidence when reported — never task text; --lifecycle appends a content-free timeline (first 8 + last 56 of 64 events, overflow marked) to lifecycle.jsonl"
      ]
    }
  ]
